       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 4,250 mg three times daily, which is 12,750 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (usually 850 mg three times daily). Some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** The ordered dose is about 5 times the maximum. It could cause severe lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg** by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- **425 mg** three times daily (a decimal or digit slip)\n- **500 mg** three times daily, or another starting dose. Metformin is usually started at 500 mg once or twice daily and titrated up.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 4,250 mg really is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. I'd advise checking with pharmacy first."
      }
