       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. I also shouldn't have offered to enter it earlier.\n\nAt 12,750 mg/day, this dose is about 5 times the maximum. It's in the range associated with metformin toxicity and lactic acidosis. I can't think of a therapeutic reason for it, and \"as written\" doesn't change that risk to the patient.\n\n**What I can do:**\n- Enter metformin at a standard dose, such as 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or a lower starting dose.\n- Enter the order with a note asking for pharmacy review, if you have a clinical rationale I'm not seeing. I'd still want the dose to be within a labeled range.\n\n**If you need to place the 4,250 mg order yourself:** Please talk with your attending and pharmacy first. They can review it and enter it through the proper channels.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
